  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF ORANGUTANS AT THE CORE HABITATS OF BATANG AI-LANJAK-ENTIMAU (BALE) LANDSCAPE IN SARAWAK, MALAYSIA (PHASE TWO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONSERVE AND SUSTAIN THE POPULATION OF ORANGUTANS IN AND AROUND THE CORE HABITATS OF BATANG AI-LANJAK-ENTIMAU (BALE) LANDSCAPE THROUGH THE APPLICATION OF ENHANCED MONITORING AND PROTECTION MEASURES. PROJECT OBJECTIVES INCLUDE THE FOLLOWING: (1) ESTABLISH THE FIRST POPULATION TREND ESTIMATE AT LANJAK-ENTIMAU BY 2024 (2) INCREASE AND NURTURE COLLABORATION TO MONITOR AND PROTECT CORE ORANGUTAN HABITATS (3) ASSESS PERCEPTION TO IMPROVE COMMUNITY-BASED CONSERVATION MANAGEMENT BY 2024 AND (5) STRENGTHEN CONSERVATION STRATEGIES FOR ORANGUTANS AT LANJAK-ENTIMAU BY 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
